CAT = "maceRole"; SEG = "ROL"
Q = [
('Under the NCSBN model curriculum, a certified medication aide gives medications under the supervision of whom?',
 'A licensed nurse', ['The physician', 'The consultant pharmacist', 'A senior nurse aide'],
 'The MA-C model curriculum places the medication aide under the supervision of a licensed nurse, who stays accountable for delegating medication tasks. Scope details are set by each state.'),
('An order reads acetaminophen every 6 hours as needed for pain. Under the model curriculum, whose judgment decides that a dose is needed now?',
 "The licensed nurse's", ["The medication aide's", "The prescriber's, at each dose", "The aide's, after asking the resident"],
 'Nursing judgment about giving a PRN medication cannot be delegated to the medication aide under the model curriculum. The aide may give the dose once the nurse has made that call, as facility policy allows.'),
('An order is written in grains, but the bottle label is in milligrams. What should the medication aide do?',
 'Have the nurse sort it out', ['Use the label dose', 'Give one tablet, then tell the nurse', 'Convert it with a wall chart'],
 'The model curriculum says the medication aide does not convert or calculate dosages. A mismatch between the order and the label goes to the nurse before any dose is given.'),
("Under the NCSBN model curriculum, which route is outside the medication aide's role?",
 'Gastrostomy tube', ['Eye drops', 'Rectal suppository', 'Transdermal patch'],
 'The model curriculum excludes parenteral routes and enteral routes through nasogastric, gastrostomy or jejunostomy tubes. Sublingual, rectal and transdermal routes are on the list of routes an aide learns.'),
("A nurse has delegated a stable resident's scheduled vitamin tablet by mouth. Who gives it during the medication pass?",
 'The medication aide', ['The nurse, every time', 'The CNA assigned to her', 'The nurse, as it is a supplement'],
 'Scheduled oral medications that a licensed nurse delegates are the core of the MA-C role in the model curriculum. The nurse stays responsible for supervising.'),
('A resident whose condition has been changing all morning is due for medications. Under the model curriculum, who gives them?',
 'The nurse, not the aide', ['The aide, with extra checks', 'The aide, once the nurse signs', 'The aide, after a pulse check'],
 "The model curriculum says an MA-C shall not administer medication when the client is not stable or has changing needs, so the nurse handles that client's medications."),
('The supervising nurse has left the building and no nurse is available to monitor clients. What does the model curriculum say about the aide giving medications?',
 'Wait until a nurse can monitor', ['Give only the scheduled oral doses', 'Give them, then call the nurse', 'Give them if a CNA watches'],
 "An MA-C shall not administer a medication when the supervising nurse is unavailable to monitor the client's progress and the medication's effect."),
("A nurse delegates a resident's morning medications to a medication aide, who then gets busy. May the aide pass the task to a nursing assistant?",
 'No, it cannot be redelegated', ['Yes, if the assistant is a CNA', 'Yes, if the nurse is told after', 'Yes, for oral doses only'],
 'A task delegated to assistive personnel cannot be redelegated by them. The aide tells the nurse, who decides how the task is covered.'),
('An aide has given eye drops to one resident many times. A nurse asks the aide to give eye drops to a new resident. Which statement about delegation is correct?',
 'It is client specific', ['It covers every resident', 'It follows the task', 'It lasts for the year'],
 'The model curriculum says delegation is client specific and situation specific. Doing a task for one client does not mean the aide may do it for every client.'),
('A nurse asks a medication aide to use an inhaler device the aide was never trained on. What should the aide do?',
 'Ask for training first', ['Watch a video, then use it', 'Have the resident show the steps', 'Use it once with care'],
 'The aide should not accept a delegation known to be beyond their knowledge and skills, and is expected to speak up and ask for training or assistance.'),
('Which task does the model curriculum say may not be delegated to a medication aide?',
 'Assessing need for a drug', ['Charting a dose on the MAR', 'Giving a scheduled tablet', 'Applying an ordered cream'],
 "Assessment of the client's need for, or response to, medication stays with the licensed nurse. Charting doses, giving scheduled oral medications and applying topical medications are aide tasks."),
("When a nurse delegates medication administration to a medication aide, who keeps responsibility for the client's overall nursing care?",
 'The delegating nurse', ['The medication aide', 'The consultant pharmacist', "The client's physician"],
 'The model curriculum says the nurse continues to have responsibility for the overall nursing care. The aide is accountable for doing the delegated task correctly.'),
('Under the model curriculum, who decides how closely a medication aide is supervised and how available the nurse must be?',
 'The supervising nurse', ['The facility administrator', 'The board of nursing, case by case', 'The medication aide, by her comfort'],
 'The nurse must determine the level of supervision, monitoring and accessibility she or he provides for nursing assistive personnel.'),
("In a facility, who is responsible for validating a medication aide's credentials and qualifications?",
 'Nursing administration', ['The delegating nurse', 'The medication aide herself', 'The consultant pharmacist'],
 "The model curriculum says nursing administration, typically through human resources, validates employees' credentials, so a nurse delegating for the first time can rely on them."),
('A medication aide believes a delegated task would be unsafe for a resident today. What is the aide expected to do?',
 'Speak up before doing it', ['Do it and chart a concern', 'Do it, then tell the nurse', 'Skip it and tell the nurse later'],
 'Aides are expected to speak up, ask for help or ask not to be delegated a task. Silently skipping it leaves the resident without care and the nurse unaware.'),
("Which of these tasks fits the medication aide's role under the model curriculum?",
 'Giving a scheduled pill', ['Giving an intramuscular shot', 'Flushing a feeding tube', 'Working out a dose by weight'],
 'Scheduled oral medications are a core aide task. Injections, feeding tube routes and dose calculations are excluded by the model curriculum.'),
("A resident asks the medication aide whether a new heart pill is the right choice for her. What fits the aide's role?",
 'Pass it on to the nurse', ['Explain why it was chosen', 'Tell the nurse next week', 'Look it up and explain it'],
 'Educating the client and judging whether a medication suits them are nursing functions in the model curriculum. The aide passes the question to the nurse.'),
('Under the model curriculum, which condition must be met before a medication aide gives a medication?',
 'A nurse assigned the task', ['The pharmacy filled it', 'The resident asked for it', 'Another aide set it up'],
 "An MA-C may administer when the assignment is to give medications under a licensed nurse's supervision and the delegation is not prohibited by law and rules."),
("A stable resident's scheduled 8 a.m. tablet has passed all three safety checks, and the nurse is on the unit. What does the aide do?",
 'Give it as ordered', ['Hold it for the nurse', 'Wait for a recheck', 'Ask the nurse to give it'],
 'With the order, label and client confirmed and a nurse available to supervise, giving a scheduled oral dose is exactly the task delegated to the aide. Holding it would make the dose late.'),
('Several state laws allow medication aides to do more or less than the NCSBN model curriculum. Where does an aide find what is allowed where they work?',
 "The state's own rules", ['The NCSBN model curriculum', "The facility's drug guide", 'Her training course notes'],
 "The model curriculum is a model that boards adopt in full or adapt, so what an aide may do varies by state. The board of nursing's rules and facility policy set the limits."),
]
